From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO for Windows: accent colors

The accent colors of the Android app (CromIKO-Accent-Color.patch) in
Customize Chrome on the desktop (the side panel and the new tab page): the
11 CromIKO colors that go with the charcoal mascot first, Periwinkle (the
default of CromIKO-Windows.patch), Lavender, Grape, Rose, Coral, Amber,
Lime, Mint, Teal, Sky and Slate, then the muted colors of Chromium (cool
grey, grey, viridian, apricot and pink). Chromium's bright colors are left
out: they are close to the CromIKO ones.

Like Chromium's colors, each one colors the whole browser from its seed
(tonal spot, and neutral for Slate), in light and dark.

License: GPL-3.0-only - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-3.0-only.html
